# =============================================================================
# .env — committed defaults for the digital-matrix blog
# =============================================================================
# This file is checked into git. Local-only overrides go in .env.local
# (gitignored). Vercel-prod overrides go in the Vercel project settings UI.
#
# Vite only exposes variables prefixed `VITE_` to client-side code. Anything
# else stays server-side at build time. Never put secrets here — this file
# ships in the public repo.
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VITE_MOTION_OVERRIDE
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Forces the device-tier motion policy to a fixed state for every visitor.
# Layered config — see src/lib/motion-config.ts for the full precedence chain.
#
# Values:
#   on    — animations forced ON regardless of tier (mobile/tablet animate too)
#   off   — animations forced OFF regardless of tier (desktop is static too)
#   <unset> — honour tier defaults (desktop=on, mobile/tablet=off). Default.
#
# A per-browser localStorage value of "on" or "off" wins over this setting.
# See src/lib/motion-config.ts for usage.
#
# Uncomment the line below to flip the build-time default:
VITE_MOTION_OVERRIDE=on

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VITE_VERCEL_ENV  (auto-bridged from Vercel's VERCEL_ENV during build)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Identifies which Vercel environment a build belongs to. Used by the blog's
# draft visibility logic in src/features/blog/data.ts:getVisiblePosts.
#
# Possible values during a Vercel build:
#   production — main domain deploy. Hides posts marked draft:true.
#   preview    — PR / branch preview deploy. Shows drafts so the author can
#                review unpublished content on the preview URL.
#   development — `vercel dev` locally. Treated like preview.
#
# Locally (npm run build), VERCEL_ENV is unset; the bridge passes an empty
# string, which falls through to "preview" semantics (drafts visible). The
# play wright.prod-contract.config.ts spec explicitly forces this var to
# "production" so the production-hide-drafts contract can be exercised
# without a real Vercel deploy.
#
# This variable is set automatically by the build script; do NOT set it
# manually unless you want to override the inferred mode.
# VITE_VERCEL_ENV=preview
